- **Coverage of new surfaces:**
  - `Verdict` / `ReportState` / `SloTier` / `Scenario` / `PId` (pure data types; no external-input boundary wired this chunk) → validation {n/a — garde deferred to the Config-validation chunk per plan; nothing deserializes from external input yet} · instrumentation {n/a — no operations/spans} · PII {n/a — no PII fields, no logging} · tests {unit✓ — 10 tests: serde round-trip + canonical names + `SloTier` wire forms + accessors + Scenario round-trip} · a11y {n/a — no UI} · tokens {n/a — no color/glyph values in core; `status_prefix()` is ASCII; state→color/glyph mapping documented in doc-comments, rendering deferred to cli/GUI}
  - `CoreError` (harness-fault type) → validation {n/a} · instrumentation {n/a} · PII {n/a — message carries no host path / struct name} · tests {unit✓ — Display + verdict/error-wall assertion} · a11y {n/a} · tokens {n/a}

- (tests) `cargo test -p conductor-core` returns 0 — existing serde round-trip tests plus the new
  positive/negative validation matrix and the path-guard tests all pass (per test-plan §4 unit strategy;
  test-runner is `cargo test`, not nextest, this chunk).

- The **typography role scale** (Display / Heading / Body / Label / Code / Data — sizes, weights,
  tracking from `design-system.md` §Typography) expressible from `--font-mono` / `--font-sans`;
  ligatures OFF for ID legibility; `tabular-nums` for the Data tier.

- **NOT** actual OTLP emission to `:4317` (Epoch 3) — the journal writer is the infrastructure;
  emission primitives extend the journal later (`EmissionSpec` is `#[non_exhaustive]` for exactly
  this forward-compat).

9. **Tests** (`#[tokio::test(flavor="current_thread", start_paused=true)]` + `tokio::time::advance`; rstest
   fixture for a seeded timeline):
   - **determinism** — same `(timeline, seed)` ⇒ identical `PhaseTransition` sequence + identical jittered gap deltas;
   - **seed-sensitivity** — a different seed ⇒ a different jitter sequence (still reproducible on re-run);
   - **timing** — each gap lands at `base ± jitter` within the declared bound; assert via `advance`, never real wall-clock;
   - **clamp/bound** — jitter never yields a negative gap and respects the bound;
   - **(optional) insta golden** — snapshot the transition sequence for a fixed `(timeline, seed)` (assert mode, no auto-write).

- **Research files inspected:** `conductor-0.1.0/chunks/2026-06-16-seeded-phase-scheduler/research.md`;
  `.andromeda/context/dependency-tree.md` + `api-surface.md`; `crates/conductor-timeline/{lib.rs,Cargo.toml}`,
  `Cargo.toml` (workspace), `crates/conductor-cli/src/main.rs`, `crates/conductor-core/{Cargo.toml,src/obs.rs}`.

- **Amendment history:** 2026-06-14-cargo-workspace-scaffold (MSRV → 1.94.1, workspace `rust-version`);
  2026-06-15-dependency-audit-gate (cargo-audit / cargo-deny floors — apply to the new RNG dep);
  2026-06-16-test-framework-fixtures-coverage-tooling (nextest / llvm-cov are reference floors, Cargo.lock
  authoritative); 2026-06-15-structured-logging-stack + log-error-boundary-redaction (the span `target` field is
  preserved by the redaction allowlist — do not over-redact).

- **Typed `thiserror` enum per seam** — define a `TimelineError` (thiserror 2.0.18) for harness faults only;
  outcomes are values / `Result::Err` is harness-only (verdict-error wall), mirroring `conductor-core::CoreError`.
  No `panic!`, no `unsafe` (security extract; `.claude/rules/security.md`).

- **Determinism test idiom** — `#[tokio::test(flavor="current_thread", start_paused=true)]` + `tokio::time::advance`;
  assert ordering/shape + virtual-clock gap placement, never real wall-clock (`.claude/rules/testing.md`
  §Determinism; test-plan §4). Needs tokio dev-features `test-util` + `macros` (+ `rt`,`time`).

- A scheduler module (e.g. `src/scheduler.rs`) — the seeded phase scheduler: an `async fn` that sequences an
  ordered phase list on `tokio::time::sleep`, holds a seeded `ChaCha8Rng`, surfaces `PhaseTransition` events;
  `TimelineError`.

- (security) The fixture deserializes via `Scenario::from_toml_str` with garde validation green (no silent parse);
  insta runs **assert-mode in CI** (no auto-write); committed `.snap` + `proptest-regressions/` are tracked (per
  security-plan §Input Validation; test-plan §4).

- **Async-in-proptest pitfall.** `prop_assert*` must run inside a closure returning `Result<_, TestCaseError>`;
  return `Ok(())` from the `block_on` async block and propagate with `?`. Do not use plain `assert_eq!` inside
  proptest (it panics instead of shrinking).

- (arch/tests) **Deterministic under seed:** same seed ⇒ identical span-tree shape (ids + linkage + status);
  ≥2 seeds ⇒ divergent identity; `ChaCha8Rng`/`seed_from_u64` cross-platform-stable; wall-clock `start/end`
  excluded from the lock (per arch §Cross-cutting Patterns + testing rules).

- (obs/security) Corpus values are NOT written to `tracing` self-obs and NOT leaked into run-report artifacts;
  emit spans stay within the bounded set (`emit.batch` / `emit.logs_batch`) (per obs-plan §11; security-plan
  §Error Handling).

- (tests) `cargo nextest run -p conductor-emit` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --profile ci` return 0;
  `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean; `cargo test -p conductor-emit --doc` returns 0;
  `cargo llvm-cov` meets the Minimal-tier line threshold (test-plan §10).

- **Crate:** `conductor-emit` (Epoch 3). Composes the existing `pub(crate)` resource/span primitives
  (`message.rs`), the exception-event builder (`exception.rs`), and the log-record builder (`logs.rs`);
  reuses `TraceEmitter`/`LogsEmitter` + `EmitError` for egress.

- **Determinism contract** — abrupt-silence is deterministic / seed-independent by construction (no seed
  param); tested as such — NOT a seed `different-seeds-diverge` test (there is no seed to drive divergence;
  same rationale as the gap, per testing-rule 2026-06-16/2026-06-18).

6. **Tests** (in-module `#[cfg(test)]`, rate.rs/port_occupier style):
   - constructor: a valid gap (e.g. 25s) → `Ok`; the boundary (exactly 20s → `Err`; just over 20s → `Ok`);
     the ceiling boundary; cf. `RateCurve::constructors_validate` (rate.rs:167-176) + `gap_bound_is_enforced`
     (phase_spec.rs:100-104).
   - exactness/determinism: `EmissionGap::new(d)?.gap() == d` for several `d` (input materially drives output;
     the seed-less analogue of the both-directions rule, test-plan §7);
   - the `FaultError` Display+source test for the new variant(s), mirroring error.rs:28-38.
   - a **doctest** on the constructor is encouraged here — unlike port_occupier (whose doctest would bind
     `:4317`), `EmissionGap` has no side effects, so a `///` example doubles as a usage smoke + coverage.

- **Determinism by construction (exact)** — the gap is a fixed value, reproducible across platforms/versions;
  the configured duration (not a seed) materially drives the output, so it is **seed-independent** like the
  exception-fingerprint primitive. The project determinism bar is satisfied trivially by exactness.

- **No new *external* dependency** — confirmed at plan time: the occupier uses sync `std::net` (no `tokio`);
  the typed bind-failure adds `thiserror` (already a workspace dependency — used by `conductor-emit`/`conductor-core`,
  so no new supply-chain/advisory surface). `tracing` instrumentation is deferred (Epoch 7).

- (arch) Ceiling is inclusive — `new(MAX_WINDOW, MAX_WINDOW)` is `Ok` (covers the Epoch-7 lunch 3600s quiet);
  `new(MAX_WINDOW + 1ms, _)` and `new(_, MAX_WINDOW + 1ms)` are `Err(WindowTooLong)` (per arch §Established
  Decisions — parity with `EmissionGap`'s `MAX_GAP` boundary tests).

- Research files: `chunks/2026-06-21-coverage-matrix-generator/research.md`; inspected `crates/conductor-report/src/report.rs`,
  `crates/conductor-core/src/{lamp,run_record,lib}.rs`, `crates/conductor-report/src/lib.rs`, both `Cargo.toml`;
  refs seed `.andromeda/refs/capability-verification-matrix.json`.

2. **Concrete comparison kinds** (the deferred piece) — the closed set of ways an `observed` value is
   compared against its `expected` target to yield `matched: bool`, drawn from the spec sources. The
   anticipated kinds (to be confirmed in planning against the specialist extracts):
   - exact equality (deterministic hard signals);
   - membership / contains (incident present in `query_incident_list`, fingerprint ∈ set);
   - presence / absence (a field/flag is set);
   - numeric ordering / threshold (p50 ≤ p95 ≤ p99, error-rate band);
   - count-floor (≥50-sample latency, ≥10-span error-rate) — a floor that, when unmet, routes to the
     calibration region rather than hard-failing.

3. **SLO timing model** — the tier-scaled bounded-tolerance deadline:
   - a tier over exactly `<5s` / `<20s` / `<90s` (the closed `slo_tier` enum already named in the
     run-report envelope);
   - latency measured **journal-relative** — `read_back_observed_at − journal_emitted_at`, never
     wall-clock-from-test-start, stamps from `std::time` (not the virtual clock);
   - a hardware-profile-aware tolerance band per tier (architecture §Timing-Tolerance Model);
   - the deadline outcome: **within tolerance** ⇒ the timing dimension passes; **exceeded** ⇒ a
     deterministic/hard deadline hard-fails, while a sample-count-floor / model-interpretive timing
     routes to `CalibrationRegion` (never hard-fails).

- **Seeds:** pick fresh per-scenario seeds (ch1 used a `4317NNN` scheme keyed to the P-ID, e.g. `4317001`);
  a parallel `…005`/`…006`/`…007`/`…008` scheme keeps them legible and distinct. Determinism does not require
  unique seeds across scenarios, but distinct seeds aid debuggability.

This is the **first** surface where verdict-first lamp precedence is realized (carried follow-up (c));
coverage-matrix (ch4), cli (Epoch 8) and desktop (Epoch 9) reuse the same rule, so the precedence logic
should be a shared, reusable helper rather than report-local.

- **Coverage of new surfaces:**
  - `MCP read-back client (rmcp over stdio)` → validation {metacharacter-reject✓ on data-dir; garde n/a — not scenario config, hand-validated at the spawn boundary} · instrumentation {`verify.readback*` tracing spans✓, `#[instrument]` `skip_all`} · PII {redacted✓ — `skip_all` keeps host paths / transport args out of logs} · tests {unit✓ (10 cases) + integ✓ (in-process rmcp duplex stub: negotiate 2024-11-05 + list + call)} · a11y {n/a — headless} · tokens {n/a — no UI}
  - `Sidecar spawn (andromeda-pulse-mcp, fixed path + .env)` → validation {injection-metacharacter reject✓} · instrumentation {covered by `verify.readback.connect` span} · PII {data-dir not logged✓} · tests {unit✓ (`build_command` sets only the data-dir env); live child-spawn integration deferred to preflight/boot chunk per the P4 test-depth decision} · a11y/tokens {n/a}

- **Typed error wall** — a `VerifyError` thiserror enum; rmcp client / transport / spawn errors fan into
  `VerifyError` variants along the verdict/error wall (transport-down / spawn-failure = harness `Err`;
  protocol / tool issues surface as typed values the *gate* chunk later maps to `Blocked`).

- (arch) Hold resolution is a typed **value** (`HoldResolution` / `Decision` in `Ok`), never `Result::Err`;
  the only `Err` on the path is a garde-invalid `HoldPoint` at load (`CoreError::Validation`) (verdict/error
  wall — arch + security + a11y extracts).

- keyed by **`run_id`** (with `seed` / `scenario`) — **no synthetic UUID/serial PK** is introduced; one row
  per **per-scenario-check** envelope, so the natural key spans `(run_id, scenario)` (a run drives many
  scenarios — the row grain is the check, not the run);

- **Keep classification light on instrumentation** — follow the prior chunk's "probe un-instrumented" precedent;
  avoid hot-path `info` logging (obs rule). If a tracing event is emitted for the calibration delta, use a
  bounded `verify.readback`-family name at `debug`, not a per-claim name.

- (obs) `restart-suppression`'s `name` is exactly `"restart-suppression"` (obs-plan §4 must-trace alignment);
  no new span names introduced — the `bypass_triggered`/`path_type` instrumentation is Epoch-8 runtime, not this
  chunk (per obs-plan §4/§11).

- **Research files inspected:** `crates/conductor-core/src/{scenario,expected,phase_spec}.rs`;
  `scenarios/{high-severity-log-capture,receiver-failed-port-conflict,receiver-lifecycle-state,latency-regression}.toml`;
  `crates/conductor-timeline/tests/{replay,determinism}.rs`.

- **Acceptance criteria: MET.** The 3 TOMLs deserialize + garde-validate + build a valid `PhaseTimeline`; every
  check is `class="Hard"`; zero `Scenario`/`ExpectedCheck`/`ComparisonKind`/`PhaseSpec` change; no new dependency;
  no new inbound bind (pure-egress; the port-occupier is P-003/ch1).

- **SLO tier per the asserted surfacing leg**: long-window / absence → `<90s` (receiver-lifecycle precedent);
  persistence-gated surfacing → `<20s` (latency-regression precedent, "60s-persistence warrants the middle
  tier"). RestartEvent ≤2s fits comfortably inside either.

- **Out:**
  - the live MCP read-back *run* (Epoch-8 driver / Epoch-10 E2E);
  - the suppression/bypass/floor **detection logic as evaluated runtime** — whether a burst was actually
    suppressed/surfaced is the Epoch-8 evaluator's comparison; the TOML only **declares** intent;
  - **P-013's "restart Pulse mid-training, verify histogram restoration" leg** — Conductor does **not** manage the
    Pulse process (explicit non-goal); the in-scope P-013 leg is the lunch-no-false-positive (histogram
    persistence-across-restart is a Pulse-internal property, observed only via an operator/Epoch-10 path, not
    driven here);
  - any **new fault or emit primitive** (all levers exist from Epoch 3/4);
  - the attention-cue → model-surfaced-incident interpretive layer (P-020/P-021 — severity-lifecycle, later);
  - the other Epoch-7 families; the CLI/desktop surfaces (Epoch 8/9).

- `conductor-core::{ClaimClass, ComparisonKind, SloTier}` — class (all `Hard`); comparison kinds
  (`Contains`/`CountAtLeast` for the presence legs; the **absence** kind question for the suppression legs);
  per-scenario tier.

- (tests) `cargo nextest run -p conductor-core` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --profile ci` return 0;
  `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean; `cargo test --doc -p conductor-core` 0;
  `bash scripts/agent-run.sh run` exits 0.

- **P-026 Halo Breathing Encoding** (`DriveObserve` → ManualCheck) — drive the rate-ramp/breathing emission
  curve (the `conductor-emit` `rate.rs` primitive already exists) so Pulse's halo "breathes" with throughput;
  visual/operator-checklist.

6. **`crates/conductor-core/src/scenario.rs` (`#[cfg(test)] mod tests`, tests only)** — add, mirroring the
   ch1–ch5 per-family pattern (research.md §Patterns):
   - a `severity_lifecycle_fixtures_load_and_validate` `#[rstest]` with a `#[case]` per file asserting `name`,
     `p_ids`, and non-empty `expected`;
   - `severity_tier_checks_are_calibration_region` `#[rstest]` over the 3 tier files (all checks
     `ClaimClass::CalibrationRegion`) + a `severity_tier_asserts_its_tier_token` assertion per tier
     (`Contains` "Autonomous"/"Suggested"/"Curious");
   - `incident_auto_resolution_asserts_resolved_and_new_not_reopen` (`Contains "Resolved"` Hard +
     `CountAtLeast` Hard + a `CalibrationRegion` leg present — the **first single file carrying both classes**);
   - `ack_cooldown_asserts_new_incident_after_via_count_at_least` (`CountAtLeast` Hard);
   - `severity_lifecycle_suite_is_mixed_class` — load all 5, assert the SUITE has `any(Hard)` **and**
     `any(CalibrationRegion)` (the one genuinely new guard shape — every prior family guard was `all(Hard)`).
   No production code changes.

- **`.andromeda/refs/pulse-capability-spec.md` §5 (P-019..P-023, P-060) + P-059** — THE normative source; each
  P-ID's "Conductor verification" clause is the concrete recipe (tier injection; trigger→cease→120 s→Resolved;
  ack→retrigger within/after; per-tier latency; sustained-incident multiple-interpretation).

- **Out:**
  - the live MCP read-back *run* + the actual model severity decision / latency measurement (Epoch-8 driver /
    Epoch-10 E2E);
  - the **model itself** — Conductor injects stimuli + declares expected tiers/outcomes; it does NOT judge
    hypothesis quality (the model is Pulse's, the black box under test);
  - any **new emit / fault primitive** (all stimuli exist from Epoch 3/4: error spans, error-rate ramps, latency
    shaping, fingerprint storm, abrupt-silence / emission-gap-resume);
  - **graceful-degradation / model-off** behavior (P-020's reduced mode) — the later P-045 model-off family
    (Epoch-7 ch8), referenced not authored here;
  - the **visual** legs of P-019 (halo magnitude, counter increment, dropdown placement) beyond a declared
    operator-checklist note — desktop/operator surfaces (Epoch 9 + the operator checklist), not auto-MCP;
  - the constellation / context-grounding + scrub/pipeline families (later Epoch-7 chunks); the CLI/desktop surfaces
    (Epoch 8/9).

- **Coverage of new surfaces:**
  - `conductor preflight [--json]` (new CLI verb) → validation {reuses hardened data-dir injection-reject ✓} · instrumentation {run_id-tagged tracing JSON via the existing `verify.readback.preflight` span + an info line; no new span name ✓} · PII {`data_dir` masked via `conductor_core::redact_value` ✓} · tests {cli_smoke E2E unit/e2e ✓} · a11y {ASCII `[PASS]`/`[BLOCKED]` prefix, never color-alone ✓} · tokens {n/a — cli}
  - `agent-run.{sh,ps1}` stage-flags + run_id-validation (new shell surface) → validation {`run_id` charset-checked before any `sqlite3`/path-join — no string-concat SQL on raw input ✓} · instrumentation {n/a — shell wraps the binary} · PII {n/a} · tests {smoke: `bash -n`, ps1 parse, `boot` + `run --unit` executed ✓; shell isn't nextest-covered} · a11y {ASCII output ✓} · tokens {n/a}

- `crates/conductor-emit/src/lib.rs` + `client.rs` — `probe_egress(endpoint) -> Result<(),EmitError>`;
  `TraceEmitter::connect(endpoint).await` + `.export(ExportTraceServiceRequest)`; `LogsEmitter` sibling;
  request builders (`trace_request`, `error_trace_request`, `severity_logs_request`, …) take **their own
